# Integrations

Docs: [docs/FEATURES.md](../../docs/FEATURES.md) · Skills: `skill-jira-integration.prompt.md`, Outlook/cloudflare READMEs

## Jira (tickets + projects)

- Config per org: `OrganizationJiraIntegrations` (encrypted tokens).
- Two tiers: **tickets** instance vs **projects** instance (optional separate URL/credentials).
- `Projects.JiraBoardId` links project to board when projects Jira enabled.
- Task ↔ ticket chain: `Tasks.TicketId` → `Tickets.ExternalTicketId`.
- Tokens: AES-256-CBC via `server/utils/encryption.ts` — never return raw tokens in GET.
- Batch status sync: map Jira statuses → local `TaskStatusValues` IDs.

## GitHub / Gitea

- Org-level integration tables; import issues → tasks.
- Issue number stored on task; avoid duplicate imports on re-run.
- Respect org/project permissions on import routes.

## Outlook calendar

- Microsoft Graph via tenant/client credentials in system settings.
- `GET /api/outlook-calendar/events?startDate&endDate` — used by Planning overlay.
- **Non-blocking** on planner load (background fetch + loading banner).
- Graph token cached in-memory short TTL — not Redis.

## Email → task queue

- `EmailTaskQueue` table; webhook from Cloudflare Worker ([cloudflare/README.md](../../cloudflare/README.md)).
- Import creates tasks; invalidate task/project caches on import.
- Outlook add-in: [outlook-addin/README.md](../../outlook-addin/README.md).

## API tokens

- `POST/DELETE` under `/api/api-tokens`; user-managed in Profile.
- Auth middleware accepts Bearer API token OR JWT.
- Redis caches token lookup — invalidate on revoke (`invalidateByEntity('authToken', …)`).

## Integration checklist (new code)

- [ ] Encrypt secrets at rest
- [ ] Mask secrets in GET responses
- [ ] `authenticateToken` on all routes except documented webhooks
- [ ] Webhooks: verify shared secret / signature if applicable
- [ ] Invalidate correct cache entities after imports/creates
- [ ] Portable SQL in integration queries
- [ ] User-facing errors in English

## Do not

- Log API tokens, Jira tokens, or Graph access tokens.
- Store integration secrets in frontend env vars.
- Block planner/ticket UI on slow external API — use async load + status UI.
